research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:113:`qftx-adhm-zero-fi-asd-correspondence` (A), proposed order 967.3; companion `qftx-adhm-zero-fi-asd-correspondence-examples`.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:119:Specify the round oriented S4=R4∪∞, compact-torus/spinor/quaternionic conventions, CP3→S4 twistor lines and antiholomorphic real structure, framed Hermitian U(N) bundles, based gauge group and ASD F+=0. Define the regular zero-FI raw locus stable+costable with both moments zero and the metric/real structure on its monad. Fix the exact curvature and k=−qN normalization. This is not the positive-FI stable quotient.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:151:For N>=2,k>=0 prove the T-equivariant correspondence between the regular zero-FI real moment-map quotient by U(k) (equivalently the regular complex quotient by GL(k) by the real/complex theorem) and the framed smooth finite-action ASD moduli on oriented S4 with k=−qN, with the stated framing/gauge action and smooth/tangent interface wherever used. The map is not an identification of the entire positive-FI resolution with ordinary ASD. The locally-free sheaf locus agrees through the monad/Ward dictionary; non-locally-free Gieseker boundary remains distinct.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/adhm-prerequisite-scaffold.md:159:`qftx-adhm-zero-fi-asd-correspondence-examples` (B), proposed order 967.3; companion `qftx-adhm-zero-fi-asd-correspondence`.
