        "title": "Donaldson's ADHM matrix equations in the source convention",
        "status": "draft",
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "deps": [],
        "dependency_roles": {},
        "statement": "Let $V=\\mathbb C^k$ and $W=\\mathbb C^N$ with their standard Hermitian inner products. Write $\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2\\in\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathbb C}(V)$, $P:W\\to V$, and $Q:V\\to W$. The Donaldson source convention for these four matrices is\n\n$$[\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2]+PQ=0,\\qquad [\\alpha_1,\\alpha_1^\\dagger]+[\\alpha_2,\\alpha_2^\\dagger]-PP^\\dagger+Q^\\dagger Q=0.$$\n\nThe second equality is an equality of Hermitian endomorphisms of $V$. It is an algebraic convention from the displayed source equations; it does not by itself assert the full-rank condition on the source's ADHM linear map or an identification with the run's raw moment maps.",
