        "statement": "Let $A$ be a framed unitary ASD connection on the round oriented $S^4$, let $\\mathcal E$ be its Ward bundle on $Z=\\mathbb CP^3$, and let $k=-q_N(A)$. Assume the conditional Penrose-transform input stated in the next paragraph for both $\\mathcal E$ and $\\mathcal E^\\vee$. Assume also the exact projective GAGA and line-family base-change inputs needed to regard $\\mathcal E$ as an algebraic bundle, to make its restrictions trivial on a complex-open neighbourhood of at least one real twistor line, and to apply the diagonal resolution. Finally, use the Chern-character normalization $\\operatorname{ch}(\\mathcal E)=N-kH^2$ in $A^*(\\mathbb CP^3)_\\mathbb Q$, where $H=c_1(\\mathcal O(1))$; this normalization is conditional on the twistor pullback class convention matching the framed charge.\n\nUnder these inputs,\n\n$$H^1(Z,\\mathcal E(-2))=H^1(Z,\\mathcal E^\\vee(-2))=0.$$\n\nThere is a canonical Beilinson three-term monad\n\n$$\\mathcal O_Z(-1)\\otimes U\\longrightarrow\\mathcal O_Z\\otimes K\\longrightarrow\\mathcal O_Z(1)\\otimes U',$$\n\nwhose middle cohomology is $\\mathcal E$ and whose terms are\n\n$$U=H^2(Z,\\mathcal E(-3)),\\qquad K=H^2(Z,\\mathcal E\\otimes\\Omega_Z^2),\\qquad U'=H^2(Z,\\mathcal E\\otimes\\Omega_Z^1(-1)),$$\n\nwith $\\dim U=\\dim U'=k$ and $\\dim K=2k+N$. The construction is natural in framed bundle isomorphisms and unique up to changes of bases in $U,K,U'$. If the ASD connection has a parallel subbundle, it splits orthogonally as a trivial flat summand and a summand with no nonzero parallel sections; the monad construction is additive across this splitting and uses no hypothesis $H^0(Z,\\mathcal E)=0$.",
