+- **Convention audit correction:** Donaldson’s printed §6 equations are $[\alpha_1,\alpha_2]+PQ=0$ and $C-PP^*+Q^*Q=0$, where $C=[\alpha_1,\alpha_1^*]+[\alpha_2,\alpha_2^*]$. Entrywise conjugation $(B_i=\bar\alpha_i,I=\bar P,J=\bar Q)$ gives the complex equation, but the raw real moment is $\bar C+\bar P P^T-Q^T\bar Q$, whereas the conjugated source equation is $\bar C-\bar P P^T+Q^T\bar Q$. `lem-qftx-adhm-entrywise-conjugation-does-not-match-real-moment-map` gives an explicit $(k=N=2)$ source solution with nonzero discrepancy. That example checks the two displayed algebraic equations, not the source full-rank condition. The proposed conversion is not used as a proved interface; the full quaternionic change of variables, rank/regularity test, framing and torus translation remain open. Donaldson’s self-duality orientation is reversed for this run’s $F^+=0$ and $k=-q_N$ convention.
+
