+# Batch 60 authoring notes — zero-FI ADHM/ASD correspondence
+
+## Scope and planning disposition
+
+- Run `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`, beta batch 60, owns only `qftx-adhm-zero-fi-asd-correspondence` and its examples companion.
+- The current batch manifest is `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-60.pages.json`; it has the exact eight A-page requirements and two B-page requirements from the current `research/plan-spec.json`, with all 14 item descriptors synchronized to their carriers. Batch notes, source coverage, proof contracts and cross-batch dependency rows are complete.
+- The live item graph computes batch 60 at level 2 with supplier batches 2, 5 and 59. The shared `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-dependency-levels.json` is stale: its batch-60 row records only batches 5 and 59. Batch 2 enters through the explicit Bianchi-lemma dependency of the determinant/charge proof. The owner must refresh shared scheduling state; this batch left it untouched. This is authoring priority, not a wait barrier.
+- **Design finding:** the dispatch says “design: none found,” and no dedicated design section governed this pair. The current plan row, owner authoring direction and owner ADHM scaffold were inspected for scope and prerequisite context, but the pair was scaffolded from the authoritative sources and current plan interfaces. The older `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md` concerns the distinct positive-FI ADHM-moduli page, not this pair. No design section is claimed as evidence for the authored arguments.
+- The older batch-12 consumer `thm-adhm-fixed-point-instanton-count` retains its positive-FI/Gieseker, zero-FI/ASD, and noncompact-pushforward duties. The new pair supplies the zero-FI/ASD dictionary; it does not identify the whole positive-FI quotient with ASD or discharge batch 12's independent pushforward obligation.
+
+## Planned item inventory and interface
+
+The canonical plan assigns five A items and two B examples. Seven local intermediate carriers were added to the A page before their consumers; their arguments are complete proofs or complete conditional proofs with missing inputs identified explicitly. Across the full run inventory, the final item levels are `0,3,1,4,4,4,5,5,6,7,8,9` in A-page order and `10,4` in B-page order; the dependency-level check finds no assigned-item errors.
+
+1. `def-qftx-zero-fi-regular-adhm-and-twistor-data` — define the oriented round (S^4), twistor space/real lines, framed Hermitian (U(N)) ASD data, regular zero-FI data, torus, and (k=-q_N) sign convention.
+2. `thm-qftx-framed-penrose-ward-correspondence-on-s4` — both directions of the framed unitary ASD/real holomorphic twistor-bundle transform, including reducible and flat summands.
+3. `lem-qftx-asd-twistor-vanishing-and-monad-reconstruction` — the paired (H^1(E(-2))) vanishings and normalized monad reconstruction/uniqueness, with flat summands handled before any (H^0(E)=0) use.
+4. `lem-qftx-adhm-real-monad-normalization-and-charge` — convert the real twistor monad to the exact raw matrices and moment maps, prove the regularity/invertibility interface, framing, and charge sign.
+5. `thm-qftx-zero-fi-regular-adhm-asd-correspondence` — compose the exact regular real/complex quotient, locally-free monad locus, Ward correspondence, framing, charge, and torus interfaces. It excludes the positive-FI Gieseker boundary.
+6. `ex-qftx-zero-fi-flat-framed-sector` — the (k=0) empty datum and unique framed flat sector.
+7. `ex-qftx-positive-fi-boundary-is-not-asd` — the (N=k=1) positive-FI stable but noncostable datum and its point-ideal monad.
+
+The additional A-page intermediates are `def-qftx-donaldson-adhm-matrix-convention`, `lem-qftx-adhm-entrywise-conjugation-does-not-match-real-moment-map`, `lem-qftx-u-n-determinant-flat-charge-normalization`, `lem-qftx-round-s4-positive-scalar-kernel-vanishes`, `lem-qftx-twistor-line-section-direct-image`, `lem-qftx-linear-twistor-monad-charge-normalization`, and `lem-qftx-asd-penrose-kernel-vanishing`. Their statements, exact dependencies, and complete proofs or explicit conditional gaps are in the item carriers and batch manifest.
+
+All items remain mathematical-domain items with mathematical-premise roles. Statements are uninterrupted and have references only in the immediately following references section. A/B pages contain YAML frontmatter only.
+
+## Current supplier inspection and readiness snapshot
+
+- `def-qftx-instanton-number-and-asd-sector` (batch 5) was read in full. Its exact local convention is (q_B=(8\pi^2)^{-1}\int B(F\wedge F)), and for (U(N)) with (B(X,Y)=-\operatorname{tr}_N(XY)), (q_N=-(8\pi^2)^{-1}\int\operatorname{tr}_N(F\wedge F)). The item proves integral (c_2) only for defining (SU(2)), not arbitrary (U(N)). Its current `loadStep1Record`/`step1Decision` record is hash-current `ready`; the actual item is draft, which is not by itself a gap. `thm-qftx-yang-mills-selfdual-action-bound` and the batch-5 page were also inspected; the theorem has the (q_B=0\Rightarrow F=0) boundary needed by the (k=0) example.
+- Batch 59's live manifest contains these carriers, and the current readiness snapshot was rechecked with `loadStep1Record` and `step1Decision`. `def-qftx-adhm-linear-data-stability-and-regularity` is `ready` with no in-run prerequisite; `lem-adhm-stable-quotient-and-torus-lift` is `ready` after its word-frame, properness, quotient-chart and torus-lift proof; `thm-qftx-adhm-real-complex-quotient-correspondence` is `ready` and keeps the positive-FI and regular zero-FI endpoints distinct. Their current Step 1 records were inspected and all three interfaces can be used as current suppliers.
+- `thm-qftx-projective-gaga-for-monad-data` has a current carrier, but its current Step 1 decision is `escalated`: its proof remains conditional on [A1] local analytic flatness, Cartan A/B and uniform generation, and [A2] relative direct-image comparison. `thm-qftx-framed-p2-monad-adhm-correspondence` and its supplier `lem-qftx-p2-beilinson-diagonal-and-framed-vanishing` also have current carriers; the monad proof is conditional on those exact GAGA [A1]/[A2] inputs and has a current `escalated` Step 1 decision. The P² statement identifies the locally-free sheaf locus with costable/regular data and states the dual-framing torus character. Batch 60 uses these current interfaces conditionally and records their actual escalations; it does not treat their draft status alone as a gap.
+- `thm-chern-weil-forms-represent-the-at-characteristic-classes-over-the-reals`, `def-chern-pontryagin-and-euler-characteristic-forms`, `def-chern-classes-from-the-projective-bundle-relation`, `thm-de-rham-cohomology-of-spheres`, `thm-de-rham-theorem`, and `def-axiom-of-choice` were checked at their read-only mathematical originals; pin paths/hashes are in `research/math-imports.json`. The determinant/U(1) normalization proof uses (H^2_{dR}(S^4)=0), Bianchi, the ASD equation, and the library determinant Chern-form convention; a flat determinant line is trivialized by the framing because (S^4) is simply connected.
+
+## Source reading and conventions
+
+- Donaldson, “The ADHM construction of Yang-Mills instantons,” arXiv:2205.08639, `research/.../owner-resolution/adhm-sources/donaldson.pdf` and `.txt`: read the ADHM problem, twistor/Ward transform, monad, Beilinson reconstruction, explicit matrices, and Dirac inverse discussion (printed pp. 3–12; full 15-page text was previously recorded as fetched/read in the owner dossier). The source is a roadmap in several analytic steps and quotes the Barth–Hulek monad theorem; it is not treated as a substitute for the required local proofs.
+- Nakajima–Yoshioka, “Lectures on Instanton Counting,” arXiv:math/0311058, `research/.../owner-resolution/adhm-sources/nakajima-yoshioka.pdf` and `.txt`: inspected §3.1 (printed pp. 17–19). It defines framed torsion-free sheaves on \(\mathbb P^2\), says the locally-free locus is identified with framed (SU(r)) ASD connections by Donaldson, and gives fixed-point data. It does not prove the required ADHM/ASD dictionary locally and its `SU(r)`/orientation/charge convention needs translation.
+- Atiyah–Hitchin–Singer, “Self-duality in four-dimensional Riemannian geometry,” Proc. R. Soc. A 362 (1978), DOI 10.1098/rspa.1978.0143: six publisher full-text attempts returned 403 after alternate Miami (404) and Oxford (403) copies were checked. Per-item nonuse and recovery searches are recorded in the source-resolution evidence; no mathematical claim is dropped.
+- Atiyah–Ward, “Instantons and algebraic geometry,” Commun. Math. Phys. 55 (1977), 117–124: six Springer PDF attempts returned short HTML/cookie-wall responses; alternate searches did not yield inspectable text. It is recorded as dropped only as an inaccessible source; its proof obligations remain.
+- **Convention audit correction:** Donaldson’s printed §6 equations are $[\alpha_1,\alpha_2]+PQ=0$ and $C-PP^*+Q^*Q=0$, where $C=[\alpha_1,\alpha_1^*]+[\alpha_2,\alpha_2^*]$. Entrywise conjugation $(B_i=\bar\alpha_i,I=\bar P,J=\bar Q)$ gives the complex equation, but the raw real moment is $\bar C+\bar P P^T-Q^T\bar Q$, whereas the conjugated source equation is $\bar C-\bar P P^T+Q^T\bar Q$. `lem-qftx-adhm-entrywise-conjugation-does-not-match-real-moment-map` gives an explicit $(k=N=2)$ source solution with nonzero discrepancy. That example checks the two displayed algebraic equations, not the source full-rank condition. The proposed conversion is not used as a proved interface; the full quaternionic change of variables, rank/regularity test, framing and torus translation remain open. Donaldson’s self-duality orientation is reversed for this run’s $F^+=0$ and $k=-q_N$ convention.
+
+## Final authoring status
+
+- The pair now has 14 carriers: the five planned A results, both planned B examples, and seven A-page intermediate results listed above. Both library pages contain YAML frontmatter only and have no Markdown body or summary. The batch manifest has all 14 complete item descriptors synchronized to their current statements and metadata.
+- The proof-contract file covers all 14 actual arguments. Strict contract validation passes with zero errors or warnings. The cross-batch-dependencies file is a 22-row JSON array; its scoped schema/ownership check passes with zero errors. Coverage maps all assigned items and has 21 harvested results. Donaldson and Nakajima–Yoshioka were fetched, inspected and stamped; `source-fetch-check --stamp` reports 2/4 fetch-verified and 4/4 resolved, with the two inaccessible sources recorded as documented drops after six attempts each. Their loss does not waive any proof obligation.
