+- The convention definition was corrected to state `deps: []` and `dependency_roles: {}` explicitly, and its own ready record plus the ready counterexample consumer record were refreshed. Three existing escalation records that transitively include this metadata change (`lem-qftx-adhm-real-monad-normalization-and-charge`, `thm-qftx-zero-fi-regular-adhm-asd-correspondence`, and `ex-qftx-zero-fi-flat-framed-sector`) retain their original escalation hashes. They remain escalated and were not overwritten; `step1-decisions.mjs` locks an existing escalation against non-owner replacement. Their unresolved prerequisites and dependency lists are unchanged. Owner resolution is needed if those records must be recaptured after the metadata-only change.
+
+### Owner escalation: unresolved prerequisite theory
+
+- **Real ADHM normalization A1:** no proof currently supplies the full quaternionic/real monad-to-raw block transformation while preserving both moment equations, regularity/full-rank equivalence, framing, torus weights and the charge convention. The explicit counterexample only rules out entrywise conjugation for Donaldson’s displayed equations. This gap affects `lem-qftx-adhm-real-monad-normalization-and-charge`, the final correspondence, and the zero-charge example. Proposed placement is a new proved A-page supplier (for example, a quaternionic block/moment-map identification lemma) immediately before the normalization lemma; do not accept the normalization or correspondence until its exact interface is proved.
